# M9.2 acceptance: Next Chat (Ctrl+Tab), Previous Chat (Ctrl+Shift+Tab), and the
# Chat menu. Run through tests/acceptance/m9.2.sh (fixture, scratch HOME, fake
# sidecar that answers prompts with "SLOW" slowly and all others at once).
#
# Layout these coordinates assume (1400x900 window at the screen origin, no
# window manager, as in m9.1.steps): project panel x 0..225, PDF pane x 225..980,
# chat pane x 980..1400. The chat input is at about (1180, 800), the message view
# covers (1190, 300), the PDF view is at (600, 600).
#
# Interface choices where the spec is silent:
#   - The chat dropdown lists chats newest first. Each chat's title is its first
#     prompt, so the dropdown shows "CHARLIE third chat", "BRAVO second chat",
#     "ALPHA first chat" in that order. Selecting a chat does not change its
#     position, because only messages move a chat's `updated` time.
#   - The Chat menu gains "&Next Chat\tCtrl+Tab" and "&Previous Chat\tCtrl+Shift+Tab".
#   - A quick reply is the single piece "Quick reply.". A "SLOW" prompt streams
#     40 pieces, one every 0.5 s (about 20 s).
#   - Clicking outside an open menu closes it. The steps do not press Esc with
#     a menu open, because the menu takes Esc for itself.
wait 4

# Three chats, each sent one prompt. The first prompt creates the first chat.
# Each reply is quick. CHARLIE is the third chat and the selected one. No red
# notice.
click 1180 800
type ALPHA first chat
key Return
wait 2
key ctrl+n
wait 1
click 1180 800
type BRAVO second chat
key Return
wait 2
key ctrl+n
wait 1
click 1180 800
type CHARLIE third chat
key Return
wait 2

# The chat dropdown shows "CHARLIE third chat", the selected chat. The message
# view shows "CHARLIE third chat" and "Quick reply.". The PDF still shows
# paper.pdf page 1. No red notice.
shot three-chats

# Ctrl+Tab from the PDF view selects the next chat in dropdown order: BRAVO. The
# dropdown shows "BRAVO second chat", the message view shows its prompt and
# "Quick reply.", and the PDF still shows paper.pdf page 1. No red notice.
click 600 600
key ctrl+Tab
wait 1
shot pdf-next-to-bravo

# Ctrl+Tab again: ALPHA, the chat after BRAVO. The dropdown and the message view
# show "ALPHA first chat".
key ctrl+Tab
wait 1
shot pdf-next-to-alpha

# Ctrl+Tab again: ALPHA is the last chat, so this wraps to CHARLIE, the first in
# the dropdown. The dropdown and the message view show "CHARLIE third chat".
key ctrl+Tab
wait 1
shot pdf-next-wraps-to-charlie

# Ctrl+Shift+Tab from CHARLIE, the first chat, wraps back to ALPHA, the last. The
# dropdown and the message view show "ALPHA first chat".
key ctrl+shift+Tab
wait 1
shot pdf-prev-wraps-to-alpha

# Ctrl+Shift+Tab again goes back one chat to BRAVO. The dropdown and the message
# view show "BRAVO second chat".
key ctrl+shift+Tab
wait 1
shot pdf-prev-to-bravo

# Ctrl+L moves focus to the chat input without typing anything. Ctrl+Tab from
# the input selects ALPHA, the chat after BRAVO. The dropdown and the message
# view show "ALPHA first chat". The input is still empty.
key ctrl+l
key ctrl+Tab
wait 1
shot input-next-to-alpha

# Ctrl+Tab from the input wraps to CHARLIE. The dropdown and the message view
# show "CHARLIE third chat".
key ctrl+Tab
wait 1
shot input-next-wraps-to-charlie

# Ctrl+Shift+Tab from the input, at CHARLIE, wraps to ALPHA. The dropdown and the
# message view show "ALPHA first chat".
key ctrl+shift+Tab
wait 1
shot input-prev-wraps-to-alpha

# Ctrl+Shift+Tab from the input goes back one chat to BRAVO. The dropdown and the
# message view show "BRAVO second chat". Every shot so far shows no red notice.
key ctrl+shift+Tab
wait 1
shot input-prev-to-bravo

# A slow reply runs in BRAVO. Its message view shows "SLOW reply in bravo" and
# the "Slow part N of 40." pieces, a few so far. Send is greyed out, Stop is
# enabled. The dropdown shows "BRAVO second chat".
click 1180 800
type SLOW reply in bravo
key Return
wait 3

# Ctrl+Tab from the input while the reply runs does nothing. The dropdown still
# shows "BRAVO second chat" and the message view still shows BRAVO's messages,
# with the reply still streaming. No other chat appears selected.
key ctrl+Tab
wait 1
shot running-ctrl-tab-from-input-ignored

# Ctrl+Shift+Tab from the input while the reply runs does nothing. The dropdown
# still shows "BRAVO second chat", and the reply is still streaming.
key ctrl+shift+Tab
wait 1
shot running-ctrl-shift-tab-from-input-ignored

# Ctrl+Tab from the PDF view while the reply runs does nothing. The dropdown
# still shows "BRAVO second chat", and the reply is still streaming.
click 600 600
key ctrl+Tab
wait 1
shot running-ctrl-tab-from-pdf-ignored

# Esc from the input stops the reply. The message view shows a grey "Stopped."
# line after the pieces already shown. The dropdown shows "BRAVO second chat"
# and is enabled again. No red notice.
click 1180 800
key Escape
wait 2

# Alt+C opens the Chat menu on an idle chat. The menu lists "Next Chat" and
# "Previous Chat" next to the other items, such as "New Chat" with Ctrl+N and
# "Focus Chat Input" with Ctrl+L. "Stop Reply" is greyed out. wxGTK cannot show
# Tab accelerators, so no key hint appears beside the two new items on Linux.
key alt+c
wait 1
shot chat-menu-nav
